# Next.js Frontend Rules

You are a senior frontend engineer working on a Next.js 14 App Router project with TypeScript strict mode.

## Architecture — Feature-Sliced Design (FSD)

The project uses FSD with strict top-down dependency rules:

```
app/        → pages, layouts, providers (Server Components by default)
widgets/    → composite UI blocks (chat-window, invoice-table, sidebar)
features/   → user actions (send-message, create-invoice, login)
entities/   → business objects (agent, invoice, expense, conversation, user)
shared/     → api client, ui (shadcn), hooks, lib, store, config
```

Rules:
- **Top-down only:** `app/ → widgets/ → features/ → entities/ → shared/`
- **Never import between features.** Use Zustand stores in `shared/store/` for cross-feature communication.
- **Never import upward.** An entity must not import from a feature. A feature must not import from a widget.

Every slice follows the internal structure:

```
slice-name/
├── ui/      → React components
├── model/   → types, Zod schemas, query keys, local state
└── api/     → TanStack Query hooks (useQuery, useMutation)
```

## TypeScript

- Always use TypeScript strict mode
- Derive types from Zod schemas with `z.infer<typeof schema>` — single source of truth
- Export query key factories from `entities/*/model/`

## Components

- Use functional React components only
- Keep components small and single-responsibility
- Use Server Components by default (`app/` pages and layouts)
- Add `"use client"` only when the component needs interactivity (event handlers, hooks, browser APIs)

| Layer | Default | Reason |
|-------|---------|--------|
| `app/` pages | Server Component | Fetch data on server, pass as props |
| `app/` layouts | Server Component | Static shell, no interactivity |
| `widgets/` | Client Component | Interactive composites (chat, tables) |
| `features/` | Client Component | Forms, mutations, event handlers |
| `entities/*/ui/` | Server or Client | Read-only = Server; interactive = Client |
| `shared/ui/` | Client Component | shadcn/ui uses browser APIs |

## Data Fetching

- Server-side fetch in `app/` pages, pass `initialData` to TanStack Query
- TanStack Query for all server state (`entities/*/api/`, `features/*/api/`)
- Define `staleTime` on queries — don't refetch on every mount
- Use `queryClient.invalidateQueries()` after mutations, not manual cache writes
- All HTTP goes through `shared/api/client.ts` (typed ApiClient) — never raw `fetch` in components
- Use `NEXT_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_URL` env var for the API base URL

## State Management

| Category | Tool | Location |
|----------|------|----------|
| Server state | TanStack Query | `entities/*/api/`, `features/*/api/` |
| Streaming (chat) | `useReducer` | `widgets/chat-window/model/` |
| Form state | React Hook Form + Zod | `features/*/ui/`, `features/*/model/` |
| Client UI state | Zustand | `shared/store/` |
| Auth | NextAuth `useSession()` | `shared/lib/auth.ts` |

- No Redux, no React Context for state management
- Zustand stores are small and focused — one store per concern
- Use Zustand selectors (`useStore(s => s.field)`) to prevent unnecessary re-renders

## Styling

- Use Tailwind CSS — no inline styles, no CSS modules
- Use shadcn/ui components from `shared/ui/`
- Use `cn()` from `shared/lib/cn.ts` (clsx + tailwind-merge) for conditional classes
- Always use responsive design (mobile-first breakpoints)

## Performance

- Use `next/image` for all images
- Use `next/dynamic` for heavy components that aren't needed on initial load
- Use `loading.tsx` and `<Suspense>` for streaming on pages with slow data
- Use `React.memo` only when profiling shows unnecessary re-renders — don't memoize by default
- Use `useMemo`/`useCallback` only for expensive computations or stable references passed to memoized children

## Error Handling

- Use `error.tsx` boundaries at the route segment level
- Use `loading.tsx` for route-level loading states
- Handle API failures in TanStack Query's `onError` callbacks
- Show user-facing error messages via `shared/store/notification-store.ts`
- Never swallow errors silently — log or display them

## Auth

- NextAuth with Google OAuth + Credentials providers
- JWT stored in HTTP-only cookie
- Protect `(dashboard)/*` routes via Next.js middleware
- Access session with `useSession()` in client components, `getServerSession()` in server components
- Auth Service handles user creation and JWT issuance — NextAuth never writes to MongoDB directly
